      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Inhaled corticosteroids with long acting beta 2-mimetics have become the mainstay of therapy for patients with asthma. The clinical and biological activity of the inhaled corticosteroids expressed as anti-inflammatory effect depends on their bioavailability, receptor affinity, lipophility, half-life terminal elimination and molecule value. Ciclesonide as a novel corticosteroid itself is inactive and used as prodrug form and needs to be cleaved by pulmonary esterases to acquire anti-inflammatory activity. Due to its quick initial activity, long clinical effectiveness in dose range of 100-800 micrograms/day, rather mild side effects, Ciclesonide is efficacious as a local potency anti-inflammatory drug."},
